    q: "How does PdfAndImg compress an image to an exact KB target without destroying quality?",
    a: "Instead of using a blind percentage slider, PdfAndImg runs an 8-to-12 iteration binary search algorithm (src/utils/imageCompressor.ts) inside your browser's HTML5 Canvas. It calculates the mathematically highest JPEG quantization factor and chroma subsampling ratio that fits within a 4% safety buffer just below your requested kilobyte ceiling."
  },
  {
    q: "Are my personal photographs, Aadhaar/PAN cards, and PDF documents uploaded to any server?",
    a: "Never. PdfAndImg is engineered as a 100% serverless, client-side web application. Every image compression, biometric exam resize, HEIC decoding, and PDF redaction/split operation runs strictly inside your device's volatile RAM using HTML5 Canvas, Web Workers, and WebAssembly (WASM). The moment you close your tab, all temporary memory buffers are permanently purged."
  },
  {
    q: "Why do government portals like SSC, UPSC, and IBPS reject photos compressed on standard apps?",
    a: "Government portals validate three parameters simultaneously: strict binary byte ranges (e.g., 20,480 to 51,200 bytes for 20KB–50KB), exact pixel dimensions (such as 200×230 px or 350×350 px), and pure baseline JPEG headers without progressive encoding or bulky camera EXIF metadata. PdfAndImg strips incompatible metadata and locks both pixel geometry and exact byte weight."
  },
  {
    q: "What should I do if my image is already smaller than the minimum KB required by an exam portal?",
    a: "If a portal requires a 20KB–50KB image and your cropped photo is only 11KB, use our Increase Image Size in KB tool (/increase-image-size-in-kb/) or set a higher target KB right inside the main optimizer. Our engine upscales canvas density and adjusts quantization tables to bring your file safely above the minimum floor."
  },
  {
    q: "Can I convert Apple iPhone HEIC photos or multi-page PDFs on Windows and Android?",
    a: "Yes. Our local WebAssembly HEIC decoder converts .heic and .heif bursts into standard JPG, PNG, or A4 PDF documents directly in your browser without requiring Apple software. Likewise, our PDF suite merges, splits, unlocks, and redacts PDFs on any mobile or desktop browser."
  },
  {
    q: "Is PdfAndImg completely free to use for bulk processing?",
    a: "Yes. All 60+ micro-tools on PdfAndImg are 100% free with no watermarks, no daily paywalls, and no account sign-ups. You can batch-process up to 50 images at once and download them as a single local ZIP archive."
  }
];

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": homeFaqs.map(item => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": item.q,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": item.a
