      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Every year, tens of millions of candidates, students, legal professionals, and visa applicants face an avoidable technical roadblock: <strong>automated portal file rejection</strong>. When you capture a photograph of your handwritten signature, academic marksheet, or passport headshot using a modern smartphone, the resulting file typically ranges between <strong>2.5 megabytes (MB) and 8 megabytes (MB)</strong>. Yet official recruitment systems—such as India's Staff Selection Commission (SSC), Union Public Service Commission (UPSC), Institute of Banking Personnel Selection (IBPS), National Testing Agency (NEET/JEE/CUET), Protean NSDL/UTIITSL PAN portals, and international consular visa platforms—enforce rigid byte ceilings as small as <strong>10KB, 20KB, 50KB, or 100KB</strong>.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        Traditional online image compressors were built for web designers looking to shave a vague percentage off blog graphics. They offer a generic "Quality: 70%" slider that leaves you guessing what the final file size will be, while simultaneously forcing you to upload your private identity documents to an unknown remote cloud server. <strong>PdfAndImg</strong> was engineered from the ground up to solve both problems simultaneously: replacing arbitrary percentage sliders with a deterministic <strong>Binary-Search Target-Lock Engine</strong> and executing 100% of the binary workload inside your device's local browser memory.
      </p>

      <!-- Section: How the Binary Search Algorithm Works -->
      <div class="panel" style="padding: 32px; margin: 40px 0;">
        <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin: 0 0 16px;">
          1. How Our Deterministic Binary-Search Target-Lock Algorithm Works
        </h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
          In digital imaging, the relationship between a JPEG's quantization quality parameter (q &isin; [0.01, 1.00]) and its resulting file size in bytes is non-linear and varies drastically depending on the high-frequency spatial entropy of the source image. A studio portrait against a solid white backdrop compresses very differently at q = 0.80 than a full-page 12th-grade board marksheet filled with dense typography and embossed seals.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
          When you enter a specific target—say <strong>20KB (20,480 bytes)</strong> or <strong>50KB (51,200 bytes)</strong>—into PdfAndImg, our core engine (<code>src/utils/imageCompressor.ts</code>) executes a multi-stage mathematical pipeline entirely in local RAM:
        </p>
        <ol style="padding-left: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; margin: 0;">
          <li>
            <strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">EXIF, GPS & ICC Profile Stripping:</strong> Smartphones embed up to 60KB of non-visual metadata—including GPS coordinates, camera serial numbers, thumbnail previews, and Apple Display P3 color profiles—inside the file header. By decoding the raw pixel matrix onto an HTML5 <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code> element, we strip 100% of this non-essential metadata before touching a single visible pixel.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">Alpha Channel Flattening:</strong> If you upload a transparent PNG or WebP signature, converting directly to JPEG in naive tools turns transparent pixels pitch black. Our engine pre-fills the canvas composite layer with pure photonic white (<code>#FFFFFF</code>) so signatures and portraits maintain high-contrast legibility.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">Iterative Discrete Cosine Transform (DCT) Binary Search:</strong> Rather than guessing a quality level, the engine establishes a search interval [q<sub>min</sub>, q<sub>max</sub>] and performs up to 12 binary search bisections. At each midpoint q<sub>mid</sub> = (q<sub>min</sub> + q<sub>max</sub>) / 2, it encodes a test Blob in memory and inspects its exact byte length against a <strong>96% surgical target ceiling</strong> (leaving a 4% safety margin so a 50KB target lands at ~48.2KB, never 50.1KB).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">Adaptive Smart Scaling (When Entropy Exceeds Capacity):</strong> If an image's native resolution (e.g., 4032 &times; 3024 pixels) is too large to fit inside a tiny 10KB or 20KB budget even at lower quantization, crushing quality alone creates severe 8 &times; 8 macro-blocking artifacts. Instead, PdfAndImg proportionally steps down the canvas dimensions using high-interpolation bilinear resampling while keeping the JPEG quality parameter high, preserving crisp text and facial features.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <!-- Section: Comprehensive Government & Visa Specification Reference Table -->
      <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin: 48px 0 16px;">
