      <!-- Section: Zero-Upload Privacy Architecture -->
      <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin: 48px 0 16px;">
        3. Why Zero-Server Client-Side Architecture Matters for Identity & Legal Documents
      </h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
        When you use a conventional cloud-based PDF editor or image resizer, your file is transmitted via an HTTP <code>POST</code> request to a remote virtual private server. Even if that provider promises to delete your files after a few hours, your sensitive documents—such as Aadhaar cards, passports, bank statements, medical records, German DSGVO contracts, Italian CAdES <code>.p7m</code> digital signatures, or Japanese MyNumber/Health Insurance cards—reside on third-party disks where they are vulnerable to misconfigured S3 buckets, unauthorized employee access, or data breaches.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        PdfAndImg eliminates server-side risk by eliminating the backend server entirely. Our static Multi-Page Application (MPA) delivers lightweight JavaScript and WebAssembly binaries from Cloudflare's edge network to your browser. Once the page loads, you can literally disconnect your Wi-Fi or mobile data and continue compressing images, merging PDFs, unlocking encrypted PDFs via QPDF-WASM, or irreversibly redacting confidential text layers. Your files never leave your hardware.
      </p>

